  "notes": "Transcribed from the official SCC 'Women and Gender Studies A.A. Degree - Local GE' program map, Catalog 2026-27, published August 5, 2026 (mapmaker.losrios.edu/Maps/7531/PublishedPdf). GE Pattern: SCC Local GE. Official Total Units: 61-62; this seed models the first-listed/recommended low path = 16 + 15 + 15 + 15 = 61 units (ENGL C1000 at 3 units per the official SCC English course page). Semester sums verified against the map's 16-17 / 15 / 15 / 15 headers. 4 terms (within the AA/AS 4-7 gate). Distinct from map 7767 (sacramento-city-college-aa-women-gender-studies), which is the Cal-GETC GE version of the same program. Major Elective (documented): minimum 12 units from ARTH 312, ENGLT 360, ENGLT 401, HIST C1001/C1001(H), HIST C1002/C1002(H), POLS 340, PSYC 356, PSYC 360, SOC 341, SOC 343, SOC 344, WGS 304/SOC 347. Sem 2 (choose 1 course): HIST C1001 selected (first-listed, 3 units; must take the 'Women's Emphasis' section). Sem 3 (choose 2 not already completed): ARTH 312 and ENGLT 360 selected (first-listed and next). Sem 4 (choose 1 not already completed): ENGLT 401 selected (next). ME total: HIST C1001 (3) + ARTH 312 (3) + ENGLT 360 (3) + ENGLT 401 (3) = 12 units. Students choosing HIST C1001/C1002 (or Honors) must take the 'Women's Emphasis' sections (identified in the class schedule). Choice slots: (1) GE INDIS 313 / HCD 310, Life Development Skills, SCC Local Area L7B — INDIS 313 selected (first-listed; first-time FYE students take INDIS 313, all others HCD 310 per the map note); (2) GE ENGL C1000 / ENGL 488 / ESLW 340, Academic Reading and Writing, SCC Local Area L1A — ENGL C1000 selected (3 units); (3) GE STAT C1000 / STAT C1000H, Introduction to Statistics, SCC Local Area L2 — STAT C1000 selected (4 units); (4) Maj WGS 302 / SOC 345, Global Women's Issues (3) — WGS 302 selected (first-listed). Students not placing directly in ENGL C1000 take the ENGL 80/ENGL C1000 combo; ENGL 488 requires ESL 325 with 'C' or better or placement; ESLW 340 requires ESL 325 with 'C' or better or Los Rios assessment placement. Students not placing directly in STAT C1000 take the STAT 10/STAT C1000 combo. WGS 300 fills SCC Local Area L4. Electives: any courses numbered 100-499 (see a counselor). AA/AS requirements: 60 degree-applicable units with 2.0 GPA, 12 units within Los Rios, each required course 'C' or better, SCC Local GE Areas L1A-L7B. Bachelor's-degree holders are deemed to have satisfied GE/graduation competency (per map). Women and Gender Studies, People & Society Meta Majors.",
